From 27df11bfc69d0dfb08d4ce6e1215db9cc0156465 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mika Laitio <mika.laitio@amd.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 23:58:28 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 23/23] TopK fixes and tuning for gfx90a and RDNA gpus

1) Fix TopK buffer descriptors when RDNA GPUs are used
  a) BufferResource defaults to the gfx9 resource
     word, corrupting TopK filter loads on RDNA gpus
     on some workloads.
  b) New test added to test_topk_plain.py to cover the
     failing 1024 by 4096 filter path
  c) Fix the failure by ensuring that
     src_buffer.config = CK_TILE_BUFFER_RESOURCE_3RD_DWORD;
     is always set, not only when changing kernel.
  d) Validate gfx1100 and gfx1201 output
2)  TopK tuning for gfx90a, gfx1100 and gfx1201
  a) add topk model tuning for gfx90a, gfx1100
     and gfx1200/gfx1201. Do not change the existing
     topk tuning for other existing gpus.
  b)  Tune dispatch and filter waves
    - Select radix for measured small-batch
      4096-column workloads by wave size
    - Cap Wave64 filter workgroups at four waves
    - Cache runtime wave size per host thread
  c) Limit TopK wave cap to tuned width
    - Keep the measured 4096-column improvement
    - Avoid changing unmeasured wider filter cases

Tools used:
- GPT: 5.6 Sol

Signed-off-by: Mika Laitio <mika.laitio@amd.com>
